# Reach the Corn tutorial, then MOVE, continuously. The test arm.
#
# Identical to still.pad up to t=47 -- same boot, same loads, same scene -- and
# then holds the left stick for 90 seconds so the camera and the world are in
# motion for the whole measurement window. Compare [STAGE], [FRAME-WIN],
# [APU-FRAME] and [APU-PACE] against the still.pad run at the same live=61.
#
# Held in four 25 s pushes rather than one, and in two directions, because a
# single sustained deflection can walk Corn into a wall and then the "moving"
# arm is a stationary arm with the stick pressed.
#
# The four pushes below are ADJACENT, NOT OVERLAPPING, and that is load-bearing
# rather than incidental -- this header used to say the opposite. A later
# event's stick value does NOT replace an earlier one: the apply path
# (src/input/xinput_device.c:743) writes a scripted deflection only while the
# axis is still near neutral,
#
#     if (ev->lx && st->Gamepad.sThumbLX > -4096 && st->Gamepad.sThumbLX < 4096)
#
# so an overlapping event finds the axis already at 30000 and is refused; the
# first event in FILE ORDER wins until it expires. (The same guard is what lets
# a live controller take over a scripted run, which is deliberate.) These four
# hand over cleanly because 55+25=80, 80+25=105, 105+25=130 and the window test
# is half-open -- not because replacement works. Buttons are unaffected: digital
# ones OR together and analog ones take the maximum.
#
# LUP/LRIGHT rather than a button: full deflection is 30000, well past the
# 4096 the report path uses to reject jitter.

12.0:START  13.5:START  15.0:A
20.0:START  21.5:START  23.0:A
28.0:START  29.5:START  31.0:A
36.0:START  37.5:START  39.0:A
44.0:START  45.5:START  47.0:A

55.0:LUP:25
80.0:LRIGHT:25
105.0:LUP:25
130.0:LLEFT:25
